    <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-2240" contextRef="c-23">&lt;div&gt;&lt;ol style="margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;li style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; line-height: 250%"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; line-height: 40px"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; line-height: 115%"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On June 15, 2023, the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;quot;FERC&amp;quot;) issued an Order Authorizing Abandonments and Determining Jurisdictional Status of Facilities (&amp;quot;Certificate Order&amp;quot;) authorizing Stingray Pipeline Company, L.L.C. (&amp;quot;Stingray&amp;quot;) to abandon by sale to Triton Gathering, LLC (&amp;quot;Triton&amp;quot;) the West Cameron 509 System (&amp;quot;WC 509 System&amp;quot;) in Docket Nos. CP20-528-000 and CP20-528-001, as described and conditioned in the Certificate Order and subsequent filings. Additionally, Stingray was granted authorization to abandon in place and by removal the Damaged Facilities in Docket No. CP20-528-001, as described and conditioned in the Certificate Order and subsequent filings.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.5in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Aptos&amp;quot;, sans-serif; line-height: 115%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.5in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Aptos&amp;quot;, sans-serif; line-height: 115%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On June 15, 2023, the FERC issued the Certificate Order authorizing Stingray to abandon by sale to Triton the Mainline Facilities (&amp;quot;ML Facilities&amp;quot;) in Docket No. CP20-529-000, as described and conditioned in the Certificate Order and subsequent filings.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.5in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Aptos&amp;quot;, sans-serif; line-height: 115%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.5in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Aptos&amp;quot;, sans-serif; line-height: 115%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On May 5, 2025, the FERC granted Stingray's request for an extension of time to September 30, 2027 to complete abandonment of WC 509 System and ML Facilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.5in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Aptos&amp;quot;, sans-serif; line-height: 115%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.5in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Aptos&amp;quot;, sans-serif; line-height: 115%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On July 31, 2025, Stingray notified FERC that portions of the WC 509 System to be abandoned by sale to Triton will be abandoned effective September 1, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.5in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Aptos&amp;quot;, sans-serif; line-height: 115%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.5in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Aptos&amp;quot;, sans-serif; line-height: 115%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On December 8, 2025, Stingray submitted to the FERC the accounting entries for the abandonments in accordance with Gas Plant instruction No. 5 and Gas plant purchased or sold, Account 102, of the Uniform System of Accounts.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.5in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Aptos&amp;quot;, sans-serif; line-height: 115%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol start="4" style="margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;li style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; line-height: 250%"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; line-height: 250%"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;See answer of inquiry number 3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; line-height: 250%"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; line-height: 250%"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style="margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; line-height: 250%"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; line-height: 250%"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; line-height: 250%"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; line-height: 250%"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;See page 122.1 Note F - Regulatory Matters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; line-height: 250%"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;During the reporting period, the following changes occurred:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="auto" height="auto" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1752px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="auto" height="auto" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1752px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-2242" contextRef="c-23">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE A &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;- &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;ORGANIZATION AND OPERATIONS:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Organization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;. Stingray Pipeline Company, LLC (&amp;quot;Stingray&amp;quot;), a Delaware limited liability company, is a direct subsidiary of Starfish Pipeline Company, LLC, an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer LP (&amp;quot;Energy Transfer&amp;quot;). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;. Stingray operates a regulated natural gas pipeline system that is engaged in the interstate transmission of natural gas in the Louisiana and Texas offshore Gulf of America areas of the United States and is subject to the jurisdiction of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;quot;FERC&amp;quot;). Prior to September 1, 2025, Stingray owned 335 miles of natural gas pipeline of various diameter that transports natural gas from the High Island Offshore System and the West Cameron, East Cameron, Garden Banks and Vermilion lease areas in the Gulf of America to onshore transmission systems in Louisiana. Effective September 1, 2025, Stingray completed an abandonment by sale of the West Cameron 509 System (&amp;quot;WC 509 System&amp;quot;) to Triton Gathering, L.L.C. (&amp;quot;Triton&amp;quot;), an associated company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray evaluated subsequent events through &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)"&gt;April 20, 2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;, the date on which the accompanying financial statements were available to be issued. Any material subsequent events that occurred during this time have been properly recognized and/or disclosed in these financial statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE B &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt; ESTIMATES AND SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;times new roman&amp;quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. Basi&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;times new roman&amp;quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;s of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray's financial statements have been prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which constitute a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (&amp;quot;GAAP&amp;quot;). The most significant differences between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are: (1) classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of income, and statement of cash flows, (2) certain assets and liabilities that result from the regulated ratemaking process are recorded that would not be recorded under GAAP for non-regulated entities, and (3) classification of certain purchase accounting related impacts, including purchase cost allocations that are not reflected in the financial statements presented herein. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;2. Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The preparation of financial statements requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and the accrual for and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the reporting period. Although these estimates are based on management's available knowledge of current and expected future events, actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;3. Cash and Cash Equivalents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray has a cash management agreement with Energy Transfer which authorizes Energy Transfer or its designated affiliate to provide cash management services to Stingray. At the close of each business day, the agreement allows for Stingray to transfer funds in excess of general operating purposes to Energy Transfer or if Stingray has insufficient funds to meet its general operating purposes, Energy Transfer will transfer all funds necessary to Stingray.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;4. Plant Materials and Operating Supplies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Plant materials and operating supplies are carried at the lower of weighted average cost or net realizable value. Materials transferred out of warehouses are priced at weighted average cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;5. Natural Gas Imbalances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Natural gas imbalances occur as a result of differences in volumes of natural gas received and delivered. Stingray values natural gas imbalance receivables and payables at current market price. Natural gas imbalances are settled in cash or made up in-kind subject to the terms of Stingray's tariff and generally do not impact on revenues.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;6. Gas Owed to System Gas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray accounts for Gas owed to system gas, Account 117.4, using the fixed asset accounting model established under FERC Order No. 581. Under this approach, gas owed to system gas volumes are classified as fixed assets and valued at historical cost. Encroachments upon gas owed to system gas are valued at current market prices. Stingray may sell gas owed to system gas in excess of its system operational requirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;7. Utility Plant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Additions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; Ongoing additions of utility plant are stated at original cost. Stingray capitalizes all construction-related direct labor and material costs, as well as indirect construction costs. Such indirect construction costs primarily include labor and related costs of departments associated with supporting construction activities and allowance for funds used during construction. The indirect capitalized labor and related costs are largely based upon results of periodic time studies or management reviews of time allocations, which provide an estimate of time spent supporting construction projects. The cost of replacements and betterments that extend the useful life of utility plant is also capitalized. The cost of repairs and replacements of minor utility plant items is charged to expense as incurred.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Retirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;When ordinary retirements of utility plant occur, the original cost plus cost of removal less salvage value is removed by a charge to accumulated depreciation and amortization, with no gain or loss recorded. When entire regulated operating units of utility plant are sold, the original cost and related accumulated depreciation and amortization accounts are removed, with any resulting gain or loss recorded in the statement of income.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Depreciation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; Stingray computed depreciation expense under the composite method using FERC-approved depreciation rates. For general and intangible plant, Stingray computed depreciation expense under the straight-line method using FERC-approved depreciation rates. For asset retirement obligations, Stingray computed depreciation expense using the straight-line method based on the estimated removal date.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Allowance for Funds Used During Construction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt; &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray capitalizes the cost of funds used during construction for capital projects. The rates used by Stingray are calculated pursuant to the FERC rules, which include an allowance for the cost of debt and equity funds.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;8. Asset Retirement Obligation (&amp;quot;ARO&amp;quot;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 13.5pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Legal obligations associated with the retirement of long-lived assets are recorded at fair value at the time the obligations are incurred, if a reasonable estimate of fair value can be made. Present value techniques are used which reflect assumptions such as removal and remediation costs, inflation, and profit margins that third parties would demand to settle the amount of the future obligation. Stingray did not include a market risk premium for unforeseeable circumstances in its fair value estimates because such a premium could not be reasonably estimated. Upon initial recognition of the liability, costs are capitalized as a part of the long-lived asset and depreciated over the useful life of the related asset. The liability is accreted to its present value each period with accretion being recorded to operating expense or regulatory asset, as applicable, with a corresponding increase in the carrying amount of the liability. To the extent, Stingray is permitted to collect and has reflected in its financials amounts previously collected from customers, such amounts serve to reduce what would be reflected as capitalized costs at the initial establishment of an ARO.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;9. Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Related party transactions primarily include payments for services provided by Energy Transfer and its subsidiaries. Transactions are generally allocated based on relevant criteria, including time spent, utility plant, gross margin, salaries, or other appropriate methods. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;10. Environmental Expenditures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Environmental expenditures that relate to an existing condition caused by past operations that do not contribute to current or future revenue generation are expensed. Environmental expenditures relating to current or future revenues are expensed or capitalized as appropriate. Liabilities are recorded when environmental assessments and/or clean-ups are probable and the costs can be reasonably estimated. Remediation obligations are not discounted because the timing of future cash flow streams is not predictable. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, there were no amounts accrued for future environmental expenditures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; margin-left: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;11. Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray's revenues from transportation of natural gas are based on capacity reservation charges and, to a lesser extent, commodity usage charges. Reservation revenues, recognized monthly, are based on contracted rates and capacity reserved by the customers. Revenues from commodity usage charges, also recognized monthly, are based on the volumes received from or delivered to the customer, based on Stingray's tariff. Revenues collected during the pendency of a rate proceeding may be required by the FERC to be refunded in the final order. Stingray establishes reserves for such potential refunds, as appropriate. No such reserves were required as of December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;12. Accounts Receivable and Allowance for Expected Credit Losses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray's operations are primarily concentrated in natural gas industry and its major customers' operations are in the same industry. The large numbers of customers in this energy segment may impact Stingray's overall exposure to credit risk, either positively or negatively, in that the customers may be similarly affected by changes in economic or other conditions. Stingray manages trade credit risk to mitigate credit losses and exposure to uncollectible trade receivables. Prospective and existing customers are reviewed regularly for creditworthiness based upon pre-established standards consistent with FERC filed tariffs to manage credit risk within approved tolerances. Customers that do not meet minimum credit standards are required to provide additional credit support in the form of a letter of credit, prepayment, or other forms of security.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray establishes an allowance for expected credit losses on trade receivables based on the expected ultimate recovery of these receivables and considers many factors including historical customer collection experience, general and specific economic trends, and known specific issues related to individual customers, sectors, and transactions that might impact collectability. Changes in the allowance are recorded as a component of operating expenses; reductions in the allowance are recorded when receivables are subsequently collected or written-off. Past-due receivable balances are written-off when Stingray's efforts have been unsuccessful in collecting the amount due. Stingray's allowance for expected credit losses was $0.4 million and immaterial as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The following table presents the relative contribution to Stingray's total transportation revenues from operations of each customer that comprised at least 10% of its revenues: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="auto" height="auto" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1752px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;No transportation receivables were outstanding from those customers that comprised at least 10% of its revenues.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;13. Fair Value Measurement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Th&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;e carrying amounts of accounts receivable and accounts payable approximate their fair value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;14. Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The FERC's Revised Policy Statement on Treatment of Income Taxes, Docket No. PL 17-1, states that it no longer permits master limited partnerships including a company that does not pay taxes itself and is owned by a master limited partnership, to recover an income tax allowance in their cost of service.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; margin-left: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;15. Taxes, Other Than on Income&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Taxes, other than on income primarily consist of ad valorem tax paid on the assessed value of Stingray's natural gas transmission lines based on fixed rates established by the applicable state or local taxing authorities. Ad valorem taxes are generally based on assessed property value at the beginning of each year.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;16. Preliminary Survey and Investigation Charges (PS&amp;amp;I)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;PS&amp;amp;I expenditures relate to preliminary surveys, plans, investigations, and similar items to determine the feasibility of projects under contemplation. If construction results, the charges are transferred to the appropriate utility plant account. If the work is abandoned, the charges are transferred to other deductions, or the appropriate operating expense account. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, Stingray has PS&amp;amp;I charges of $22.5 million.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b style="background-color: unset; text-align: inherit; font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;17. Commitments and Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray is subject to proceedings, lawsuits and other claims related to environmental and other matters. Accounting for contingencies requires significant judgment by management regarding the estimated probabilities and ranges of exposure to potential liability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE C &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;- &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS: &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Related party transactions primarily include payments for services provided by Energy Transfer and other associated companies. For each of the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, corporate charges and shared services were $1.1 million, reported in operating expenses on the statement of income.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Accounts receivable from and accounts payable to associated companies are primarily related to the cash management activity and operating and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;administrative services provided by Energy Transfer and its subsidiaries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE D &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;- &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;UTILITY PLANT:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 31.5pt; text-indent: 9pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The following table provides a summary of utility plant at the dates indicated:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="auto" height="auto" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1752px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE E - ASSET RETIREMENT OBLIGATIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 27pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray's recorded AROs are primarily related to owned offshore lines and platforms. The present value of the estimated asset retirement costs has been capitalized as part of the carrying amount of the related long-lived assets, which was $35.1 million and $92.0 million as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. Stingray has evaluated 17 platforms and pipelines and has determined a range of abandonment dates through December 2035. A total of 10 platforms and pipelines were abandoned as of December 31, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The following table is a reconciliation of the carrying amount of the ARO liability reflected as liabilities on the balance sheet for the periods presented. The ARO liability is recorded in Asset retirement obligations, Account 230. Changes in assumptions regarding the timing, amount, and probabilities associated with the expected cash flows, as well as the difference in actual versus estimated costs, could result in a change in the amount of the liability recognized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="auto" height="auto" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1752px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt;  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; margin-left: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; margin-left: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE F - REGULATORY MATTERS,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMMITMENTS, CONTINGENCIES AND ENVIRONMENTAL LIABILITIES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Regulatory Matters. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On June 15, 2023, the FERC issued an &amp;quot;Order Authorizing Abandonments and Determining Jurisdictional Status of Facilities&amp;quot; in Stingray's abandonment proceeding in Docket Nos. CP20-528-000, CP20-528-001 and CP20-529-000(&amp;quot;June 15, 2023 Order&amp;quot;). In the June 15, 2023 Order, the FERC granted Stingray's requests to: (i) abandon the WC 509 System by sale to Triton and also by removal and in-place; (ii) abandon the Mainline Facilities by sale to Triton; (iii) abandon its Natural Gas Act section 7 certificate of public convenience and necessity for the operation of its pipeline system; (iv) abandon its blanket certificate issued under Part 157; (v) abandon its Part 284 blanket certificate; and (vi) cancel its FERC Gas Tariff. The FERC also determined that the WC 509 System will be non-jurisdictional once acquired by Triton. Subsequently, on July 17, 2023, Stingray requested rehearing of the condition in Ordering Paragraph (H), requiring Stingray to either place Segment 3394 into service or obtain shipper agreement that it remains out of service, which was denied. Stingray filed an appeal on that issue, submitted briefs and oral argument was held on October 18, 2024. The Court of Appeals denied Stingray's petition by order issued on December 20, 2024. On July 31, 2025, Stingray filed with the FERC, a notice of abandonment of the WC 509 System to be effective September 1, 2025, by sale to Triton. The abandonment by sale was completed on September 1, 2025. On December 8, 2025, Stingray submitted Journal entries to the FERC for the sale of certain facilities to Triton and was approved on January 12, 2026, Docket No. AC26-11-00.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Liabilities for Litigation and Other Claims&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;i&gt;.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; Stingray records accrued liabilities for litigation and other claim costs when management believes a loss is probable and reasonably estimable. When management believes there is at least a reasonable possibility that a material loss or an additional material loss may have been incurred, Stingray discloses (i) an estimate of the possible loss or range of loss in excess of the amount accrued; or (ii) a statement that such an estimate cannot be made. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, Stingray had no recorded litigation or other claim-related accrued liabilities. Stingray does not have any material litigation or other claim contingency matters assessed as probable or reasonably possible that would require disclosure in the financial statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 31.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Environmental Matters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;i&gt;.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray's operations are subject to extensive federal, state and local environmental and safety laws and regulations that require expenditures to ensure compliance, including related to air emissions and wastewater discharges, at operating facilities and for remediation at current and former facilities as well as waste disposal sites. Historically, Stingray's environmental compliance costs have not had a material adverse effect on its results of operations but there can be no assurance that such costs will not be material in the future or that such future compliance with existing, amended or new legal requirements will not have a material adverse effect on Stingray's business and operating results. Costs of planning, designing, constructing and operating pipelines and other facilities must incorporate compliance with environmental laws and regulations and safety standards. Failure to comply with these laws and regulations may result in the assessment of administrative, civil and criminal penalties, the imposition of investigatory, remedial and corrective action obligations, natural resource damages, the issuance of injunctions in affected areas and the filing of federally authorized citizen suits. Contingent losses related to all significant known environmental matters have been accrued and/or separately disclosed. However, Stingray may revise accrual amounts prior to resolution of a particular contingency based on changes in facts and circumstances or changes in the expected outcome.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Environmental exposures and liabilities are difficult to assess and estimate due to unknown factors such as the magnitude of possible contamination, the timing and extent of remediation, the determination of Stingray's liability in proportion to other parties, improvements in cleanup technologies and the extent to which environmental laws and regulations may change in the future. Although environmental costs may have a significant impact on Stingray's results of operations for any single period, Stingray believes that such costs will not have a material adverse effect on its financial position.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Air Quality Standards. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;In 2023, the United States Environmental Protection Agency (&amp;quot;EPA&amp;quot;) finalized its Good Neighbor Plan (the &amp;quot;Plan&amp;quot;) which seeks to reduce nitrogen oxide pollution from power plants and other industrial facilities from 23 upwind states which the EPA determined is contributing to National Ambient Air Quality Standards (&amp;quot;NAAQS&amp;quot;) nonattainment and interfering with maintenance of the 2015 ozone NAAQS in downwind states. As part of the Plan, the EPA announced that it would be issuing prescriptive emission standards for several sectors, including certain new and existing internal combustion engines of a certain size used in pipeline transportation of natural gas. The EPA's final rule was to become effective on August 4, 2023, and the prescribed emission standards were scheduled to be effective in 2026. However, on March 12, 2025, the EPA announced plans to end the Plan. Operators and industry groups have challenged the Plan in the District of Columbia Circuit (&amp;quot;D.C. Circuit&amp;quot;), as well as the legal predicates to the individual upwind states' inclusion in the Plan in the regional circuits. The effectiveness of the rule is currently stayed in certain states within Energy Transfer's footprint, by nature of judicial stays of the legal predicate to the Plan, by judicial stay of the Plan itself by the United States Supreme Court (&amp;quot;U.S. Supreme Court&amp;quot;), or by the administrative stay issued by the EPA in October 2024. On June 18, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;2025, the U.S. Supreme Court ruled that the regional circuits are the appropriate venue for the proceedings. On July 30, 2025, the United States Court of Appeals for the Tenth Circuit placed the case in abeyance pending the EPA's reconsideration of its disapproval of upwind states' state implementation plans addressing their Plan obligations. Proceedings challenging the Plan in the D.C. Circuit were also placed in abeyance on May 2, 2025 pending the EPA's reconsideration of the Plan. The EPA is preparing a proposed rulemaking as part of the reconsideration process, and on January 27, 2026, the EPA announced its proposal to approve state implementation plans for certain states, including those in which Stingray operates, which would resolve those states' obligations under the Good Neighbor Plan. Stingray cannot predict with any certainty the substance of any later proposed rule or the potential impacts on Stingray.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; Stingray currently estimates that the existing final rule would require retrofitting or replacement of certain of its engines used in its operations. Compliance with the Plan (if implementation is not stayed or otherwise delayed) may require substantial capital expenditures which could adversely affect Stingray's business in future periods. However, at this time, Stingray is still assessing the potential costs of this rule and, given uncertainties resulting from the multiple legal challenges filed against the Plan in various states, in the D.C. Circuit and the U.S. Supreme Court, Stingray cannot predict with any certainty what the final costs of compliance for the Plan for Stingray ultimately may be.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Other Commitments and Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Federal Pipeline Integrity Rules&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray's pipeline operations are subject to regulation by the United States Department of Transportation under the Pipeline Hazardous Materials Safety Administration (&amp;quot;PHMSA&amp;quot;), pursuant to which PHMSA has established requirements relating to the design, installation, testing, construction, operation, replacement and management of pipeline facilities. Moreover, PHMSA, through the Office of Pipeline Safety, has promulgated a rule requiring pipeline operators to develop integrity management programs to comprehensively evaluate their pipelines, and take measures to protect pipeline segments located in what the rule refers to as &amp;quot;high consequence areas&amp;quot;. Activities under these integrity management programs involve the performance of internal pipeline inspections, pressure testing or other effective means to assess the integrity of these regulated pipeline segments, and the regulations require prompt action to address integrity issues raised by the assessment and analysis. Integrity testing and assessment of all of these assets will continue, and the results of such testing and assessment could cause Stingray to incur future capital and operating expenditures for repairs or upgrades deemed necessary to ensure the continued safe and reliable operation of Stingray; however, no estimate can be made at this time of the likely range of such expenditures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray's operations are also subject to the requirements of the Federal Occupational Safety and Health Act (&amp;quot;OSHA&amp;quot;), and comparable state laws that regulate the protection of the health and safety of employees. In addition, the Occupational Safety and Health Administration's hazardous communication standard requires that information be maintained about hazardous materials used or produced in Stingray's operations and that this information be provided to employees, state and local government authorities and citizens. Stingray believes that its past costs for OSHA required activities, including general industry standards, record keeping requirements and monitoring of occupational exposure to regulated substances have not had a material adverse effect on Stingray's results of operations; however, there is no assurance that such costs will not be material in the future.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE G - REVENUE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 31.5pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Contract Balances with Customers. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray satisfies its obligations by transferring goods or services in exchange for consideration from customers. The timing of performance may differ from the timing the associated consideration is paid to or received from the customer, thus resulting in the recognition of a contract asset or a contract liability. As of January 1, 2024, the opening balance of accounts receivable from contracts with customers was $0.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 31.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray recognizes a contract asset when making upfront consideration payments to certain customers or when providing services to customers prior to the time at which Stingray is contractually allowed to bill for such services. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, no contract assets have been recognized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 31.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray recognizes a contract liability if the customer's payment of consideration precedes Stingray's fulfillment of the performance obligations. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, no contract liabilities have been recognized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 31.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Performance Obligation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;At contract inception, Stingray assesses the goods and services promised in its contracts with customers and identifies a performance obligation for each promise to transfer a good or service (or bundle of goods or services) that is distinct. To identify the performance obligations, Stingray considers all the goods or services promised in the contract, whether explicitly stated or implied based on customary business practices. For a contract that has more than one performance obligation, Stingray allocates the total contract consideration it expects to be entitled to, to each distinct performance obligation based on a standalone-selling price basis. Revenue is recognized when (or as) the performance obligations are satisfied, that is, when the customer obtains control of the good or service. Certain of Stingray's contracts contain variable components, which, when combined with the fixed component are considered a single performance obligation. For these types of contracts, only the fixed co&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;mponent of the contracts are included in the amount of revenue expected to be recognized on contracts with customers existing as of December 31, 2025. Stingray did not have any transaction price allocated to unsatisfied (or partially satisfied) performance obligations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 31.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Practical Expedients Utilized by Stingray. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray elected the following practical expedients in accordance with Accounting Standards Codification Topic 606:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style="margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Right to invoice &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;- Stingray elected to utilize an output method to recognize revenue that is based on the amount to which Stingray has a right to invoice a customer for services performed to date, if that amount corresponds directly with the value provided to the customer for the related performance or its obligation completed to date. As such, Stingray recognized revenue in the amount to which it had the right to invoice customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style="margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Significant financing component &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;- Stingray elected not to adjust the promised amount of consideration for the effects of significant financing component if Stingray expects, at contract inception, that the period between the transfer of a promised good or service to a customer and when the customer pays for that good or service will be one year or less.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Unearned variable consideration - &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Stingray elected to only disclose the unearned fixed consideration associated with unsatisfied performance obligations related to Stingray's various customer contracts which contain both fixed and variable components.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 5pt 0 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 5pt 0 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE H - SUPPLEMENTAL CASH FLOW INFORMATION:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 5pt 0 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="auto" height="auto" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1752px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
